  "critic_analysis": "The Actor Harness exhibits three tightly coupled failure patterns across at least 15 incorrect cases. Pattern A: the agent answers only one part of a multi-part question, ignoring the remaining entities (e.g., only searched for one of two locations, only confirmed one of two magazines). Pattern B: the agent answers from its own incorrect knowledge with zero tool calls. Pattern C: the agent makes one compound query, fails to retrieve the direct answer, then gives up instead of issuing a follow-up query. There are no retriever errors (0%), no static answer coverage gaps, and the corpus contains the needed evidence for the cases inspected. The root cause is that the system prompt and extension instruction do not teach the agent to decompose multi-part questions into separate targeted queries, to issue follow-up queries when a result is incomplete, or to verify coverage of all question elements before finalizing. The enabled `result_summary_prompt` extension injects a vague instruction ('expand the search scope and increase the recall quantity') after every tool call, but this is too generic and does not guide the agent to identify missing sub-questions.",
  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "The Harness lacks decomposition and coverage verification instructions in its system prompt.",
    "observed_pattern": "Across at least 8 incorrect cases, the agent searches for only one entity in a multi-entity question and stops. Across at least 10 cases, the agent makes one compound search query, gets partial results (e.g., winner name without birth year) and gives up rather than issuing a follow-up query. Across at least 3 cases, the agent answers with zero tool calls using incorrect knowledge.",
    "excluded_causes": [
      "Retriever errors (0% rate in the evaluation report)",
      "Unsupported evidence (the inspected cases had supported evidence in the corpus)",
      "Model knowledge limitations (the model hallucinated incorrect facts instead of searching)",
      "Isolated sampling mistakes (pattern repeats across 15+ distinct cases)"
    ],
    "suggested_change": "Replace the vague 'expand the search scope' extension instruction with a structured multi-step instruction in the system prompt or extension. The instruction should specify: (1) decompose multi-part questions into separate independent queries, (2) after receiving search results, check if every sub-question is answered, (3) if a sub-question is unanswered, issue a new query for that specific entity or fact, (4) do not include information in the final answer that is unsupported by retrieved passages.",
    "expected_effect": "The agent would issue follow-up queries for unanswered sub-questions instead of stopping prematurely, and would not hallucinate missing facts, increasing accuracy on multi-part and multi-hop questions.",
    "risks": [
      "Increased tool calls per question may raise latency and token consumption",
      "Overly rigid instructions may cause the agent to search excessively for questions that already have sufficient evidence"
    ]
  },
  "harness_manifest": {
    "schema_version": 1,
    "harness_id": "baseline_search",
    "tools": [
      {
        "instance_id": "search",
